WEBVTT

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.710
This is our challenge...

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:17.290
No, it's our spirit of adventure.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:18.500
What the heck are you talking about?

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.750
Pistons embody man's spirit of adventure!

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:33.750
Go! 1,000 horsepower!

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:42.500
What?

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:34.880
Five years have passed since the Great Catastrophe.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:41.880
The reconstruction and technical innovation
it brought about offered a place for robots in our society.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:56.380
The robots do the jobs
humans have provided them without fail.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:59.250
And they have now become indispensable to humans.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.380
Here, take one.

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:10.540
Whee!

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:15.130
Ah, my balloon!

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:16.960
Here, have a balloon.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:19.920
But robots are not human.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:20.790
Here, have a balloon.

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:23.420
Robots don't have hearts.

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:25.670
Here, have a balloon.

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:30.420
Ouch! O-ow...

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:32.920
Ah, jeez, Umataro, hold still!

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:36.670
I am, aren't I? I know you can see me clenching my teeth!

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:40.630
Try patting more gently, Hiroshi.

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:43.420
I did warn you not to do that.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:48.080
Your clothes are covered in oil and
you even managed to get yourself injured...

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:54.460
Well, it is true I didn't plan for this to happen.

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:59.000
You know, Six is an artificial intelligence robot
constructed for research purposes.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.130
Why make him so ridiculously strong?

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:03.080
It's all the better he's strong!

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:04.580
And it's cool, too!

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:08.380
"Cool," huh?

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:12.580
I really like that childish side of you, Umataro, you know?

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:14.540
Calling me childish is just rude!

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:16.670
Say it's my philosophy! My philosophy!

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:23.250
He's got 1,000 horsepower! 1,000 horsepower!
That's as much as two semi trucks!

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:24.790
What you gonna use all that for?

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:28.580
Don't be silly. A106 is a research robot, alright?

00:04:29.210 --> 00:04:33.790
This robot here will make our next-generation AI
"Bewusstsein" known to the world at large.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:37.130
He needs specs that we can be proud of
no matter where we show them off!

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:41.000
I've already gone ahead and updated the version
of our experimental program.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:45.040
You mean the prototype of the beta version
of the test version of the experimental version, right?

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:46.290
Well, yeah.

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:49.210
I also greatly augmented all of the sensors!

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:52.460
I've also installed some superhero-esque logic routines!

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:53.630
And besides that...

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:56.380
What are you doing fiddling with him so much?!

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:57.130
Eh?

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:59.040
We don't even have the budget!

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:02.500
We have to show some real results
by the next faculty meeting...

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:04.000
...or we're finished!

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:06.170
"Finished...?"

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:10.630
AHH! That's right!

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:13.380
We've used up the research funds
that were earmarked for Seven,

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:15.920
the culmination of the A10 series,
so we're already down to zero!

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:17.920
That's why we got part-time jobs, right?

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:18.920
Part-time jobs!

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:21.920
Part-time jobs... That's right.

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:26.290
A101, what time is it right now?

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:27.790
It's 11 o'clock.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:30.040
It is time to leave for your part-time job.

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:33.290
Oh, to think I was worried. We've still got time...

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:35.880
We're gonna be late!

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:44.920
Tch, that's a rudimentary error of
the Bewusstsein we put inside A101, huh?

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:47.580
You mean a rudimentary error of a version of
Bewusstsein even more rudimentary than

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:51.170
the prototype of the beta version of the test version
of the experimental version, right?!

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:52.920
More importantly, we've got jobs waiting!

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:56.250
Anyway, you go on ahead, Hiroshi!

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:58.960
I'll change in a flash and be right behind you!

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.080
O-okay...

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:03.580
Alright, I'll go on ahead and get things set up!

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:06.920
Oh, I left a croquette sandwich over there,
so go ahead and eat that on your way. I'll be waiting!

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:07.830
Okay!

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:16.330
Alright.

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:19.540
A croquette sandwich from the school cafeteria, huh?

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:26.130
The interplay between the sauce and crisp croquettes
makes this thing simply exquisite!

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:28.330
Yep, yep.

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:42.380
Hurry, hurry now.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:49.130
But, you know, this croquette sandwich
really is simply the best.

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:52.130
The sauce goes so well with the soft bread...

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:55.330
It's exquisite!

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:05.630
Excuse me, I wasn't watching where I was going and...

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:09.580
Moriya Tsutsumi-san from Lab 1?!

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:11.250
Yo.

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:16.830
I can't believe I managed to collide with
the top research student at Nerima University!

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:18.670
I'm so sorry!

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:22.330
If something were to happen to
the most genius mind in all of Japan...

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:27.920
It's fine. Besides, are you alright yourself?

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:30.710
Of course, I'm perfectly fine!

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:33.210
Uh, allow me to go pick up your wheelchair!

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:35.920
No, you needn't worry about that.

00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:50.420
See?

00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:51.670
Wow!

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:56.420
Well, you should get going.

00:07:56.710 --> 00:07:58.830
From what I could tell, you're in a hurry.

00:08:00.130 --> 00:08:01.500
My part-time job! My job!

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:04.330
Oh, that's right, my croquette sandwich.
My croquette sandwich!

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:05.330
My croquette-

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:10.330
Here, your croquette sandwich from the school store.

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:12.040
Thanks.

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:14.330
You're welcome.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.630
Well then, please excuse me.

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:23.630
Eh? You aren't going to properly
acknowledge me? Jeez...

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:28.580
You got jilted, huh, Motoko?

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:34.460
Well, how about you, Big Brother?

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:38.330
Did I not just see that "never-topple robo-chair"
of yours get knocked over?

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:42.130
Yeah, seems this thing
still has some room for improvement.

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:47.880
So, who exactly is that "courageous" boy
who dirtied your chair?

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:57.380
I believe he's a graduate student from Lab 7...

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:02.960
Lab 7... The one on the far side of
the campus' West Building...?

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:05.630
Yeah.

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:08.960
He's using it together with
some weirdo named Umataro or something.

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:11.580
It's a fitting place for trash like them.

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:20.580
Hey now, Motoko, you're not getting any
funny ideas again now, are you?

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:27.210
Yeah, yeah, I know!
"Hanging around trash will get you dirty."

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:34.080
But, ridiculing the likes of that trash is pretty fun...

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:49.380
Here at Mecha City, symbol of the reconstruction,
for a limited time we're holding a collaborative event:

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:54.210
"Mayor Camecca's Corps vs. Hell's Hebihebi Devil Army"!

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:55.670
Hey, Ran!

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:56.880
Big Brother.

00:09:56.880 --> 00:09:58.000
So you came.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:58.710
Yeah.

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:00.670
Haven't seen Umataro, have you?

00:10:01.170 --> 00:10:02.790
The guy that hangs out with you?

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:03.880
Yeah, him.

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:04.880
Haven't seen him.

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:07.460
What the heck is that guy doing?

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:10.170
I mean, we finally got this high-paying gig...

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:13.130
Where's Six?

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:14.830
I left him back at Lab 7.

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:17.920
It's not like I can just bring him to my part-time job.

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:19.460
Lab 7...

00:10:20.250 --> 00:10:21.210
See ya.

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:27.460
You're after Six's parts again, aren't you?

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:28.670
Yeah.

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:33.040
No, just no. We don't have the budget
to buy any replacement parts, okay?

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:37.420
Today, just be a good girl and watch me
have my moment of glory out there.

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:39.710
Your moment, Brother?

00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:42.380
Yep, I'll be Commander Dokuron!

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:44.000
Dokuron?

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:47.380
Hello, all of you out there!

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:52.330
The mayor of Mecha City
is just about to get the parade started!

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:55.210
Uh-oh, I've gotta get going!
Well, make sure to look for me!

00:11:01.290 --> 00:11:02.750
Understood.

00:11:03.420 --> 00:11:07.710
Today we've got a full line-up
of your favorite robot wrestlers!

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:11.960
Please enjoy the show put on
by our delightful inhabitants!

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:16.080
Ah, jeez!

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:18.630
That damn Umataro isn't here yet!

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:21.710
And the parade's about to start!

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:28.330
That guy... He's supposed to be Mayor Camecca...

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:31.630
He should do whatever it takes
even if it means showing up here naked!

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:37.880
E-excuse me! I'm not used to this Dokuron costume!

00:11:46.040 --> 00:11:47.500
Umataro?

00:11:49.130 --> 00:11:51.500
Hey, Umataro!

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.130
Over here, I'm over here! Look! Come over here quick!

00:11:53.130 --> 00:11:54.500
Hey, you!

00:11:56.880 --> 00:12:00.130
It's time for you to get going! Get this thing on, get it on!

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:22.080
Maria!

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:27.710
M.D.M.! M.D.M.!

00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:35.080
M.D.M.! M.D.M.! M.D.M.!

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:38.210
Well, everyone, the wait is finally over!

00:12:38.210 --> 00:12:43.250
The parade featuring Mecha City's
delightful inhabitants starts now!

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:48.630
Everyone!

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:53.250
Are your motor coils nice and warmed up now?

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:55.670
Yeah!

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:59.170
Is your oil circulating?

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:01.330
Yeah!

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:06.250
Oh, yeah! No matter how many times
I come to Mecha City, I always get fired up!

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:19.960
Amazing!

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:26.580
They've got Dr. Lolo here! For a robo-ace champion,
she's quite the mysterious and beautiful developer!

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:31.420
The Mecha City Robot Parade... starts now!

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:38.580
Yeah!

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:55.000
Here they come!

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.040
Here they are!

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.040
Gigaton Hammer!

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:27.170
Even Mohawk Basso is here!

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:30.170
Robots, yeah!

00:14:30.460 --> 00:14:32.380
Robo-racing, yeah!

00:14:35.670 --> 00:14:38.170
The front of the parade has passed Point A.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.420
Send out General Takeuma.

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:07.040
Let's see... Ochanomizu-kun is supposed to be...

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:11.460
Oh, there, there he is. Commander Dokuron!
So he's inside there, huh?

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:15.170
His partner in Lab 7...

00:15:15.670 --> 00:15:20.920
Uh... Ushi... No, Umataro-kun is...

00:15:22.830 --> 00:15:25.000
Camecca, mayor of Mecha City?

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:26.580
Look, up there.

00:15:31.080 --> 00:15:32.290
Oh, you're right.

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:38.170
I see... So he's got the simple job
of standing up there and waving, huh?

00:15:38.380 --> 00:15:39.380
Yeah, I suppose.

00:15:40.670 --> 00:15:45.710
I'm the genius scientist you're after, Umataro Tenma.

00:15:47.290 --> 00:15:49.960
Is that photo of yours a little too touched-up?

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:52.210
It's just a case of the adjustment AI
being a piece of junk.

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:55.670
It's not like you're even who I'm after.

00:15:55.670 --> 00:15:58.040
The one I'm interested in is Ochanomizu-kun.

00:15:58.040 --> 00:16:00.330
You're lying, you little spy!

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:01.290
Eh?

00:16:02.170 --> 00:16:03.540
I know about you!

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:08.580
Aren't you the younger sister of Moriya Tsutsumi,
Lab 1's top research student?!

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:13.960
You were ordered by your brother to come here and
do recon on our totally genius research, weren't you?!

00:16:16.210 --> 00:16:17.080
What?

00:16:17.460 --> 00:16:22.540
Well, my big brother did call you a weirdo.
But you're even worse than that.

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:24.130
What did you say?!

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:26.380
That aside...

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:28.750
The fact is you're right here!

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:31.460
So who exactly is inside that mayor's costume?

00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:35.210
It's just like a spy to ask that kind of question.

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:36.380
Huh?

00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:38.880
Very well, then! I'll tell you.

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:42.750
Inside that costume...!

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:47.380
The one who is up there waving completely naturally
is none other than...!

00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:13.830
Rise in temperature detected
in General Takeuma's control block.

00:17:13.830 --> 00:17:14.630
What?!

00:17:44.880 --> 00:17:46.630
Umataro!

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:50.250
Wait up, Umataro!

00:17:52.540 --> 00:17:52.750
Operational fault. Temperature is rising inside the block.

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:55.290
Get the head usher to guide people
to the evacuation route! And don't start a panic!

00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:57.130
Controls nonresponsive. Controls nonresponsive.

00:18:07.710 --> 00:18:08.670
Incredible!

00:18:08.670 --> 00:18:12.080
They're even reproducing the Blazing Back Aura?!

00:18:26.880 --> 00:18:29.290
Wh-what is he doing?!

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:32.040
So, who is that anyway?

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:55.040
Is that...?

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:13.250
Amazing! They're even reproducing the Emerald Splash!

00:19:42.880 --> 00:19:46.040
From Nerima University? I see.

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:58.960
During a parade held at Mecha City,
a robot had some trouble and collapsed.

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:02.880
Consequently, the surrounding area
is experiencing major traffic delays,

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:06.330
Good grief! This is what you get with robots!
and the automatic traffic system
is directing cars to alternative routes...

00:20:07.040 --> 00:20:10.880
All attractions have now closed for the day.
Please take care and head home.

00:20:10.880 --> 00:20:13.290
That's super high-pressure reinforced pipe, you know.

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:17.000
He broke through that thing just by punching it.

00:20:18.130 --> 00:20:20.080
Take a look at this, Hiroshi.

00:20:20.790 --> 00:20:22.920
These are the traces of a short circuit that sparked a fire.

00:20:22.920 --> 00:20:24.250
It's still fresh...

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:27.330
It seems the fire was put out by this water here.

00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:28.880
Look further inside.

00:20:28.880 --> 00:20:30.170
Further inside?

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:37.460
Compressed hydrogen tanks!

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:43.880
So that means... it wouldn't have been much longer
until a huge explosion was triggered?

00:20:44.330 --> 00:20:47.040
And the people here would've been caught up in it?

00:20:47.580 --> 00:20:48.880
Exactly.

00:20:51.460 --> 00:20:56.380
Sensing that terrible disaster before it could occur,
and without being ordered to act by anyone...

00:20:57.210 --> 00:21:00.880
...he prevented it based on his own judgment!

00:21:02.380 --> 00:21:04.880
His own judgment...?

00:21:07.750 --> 00:21:11.290
Welcome home, A106.

00:21:19.920 --> 00:21:21.580
Our Six...

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:27.210
Our Bewusstsein theory really was sound!

00:21:27.420 --> 00:21:28.710
Naturally.

00:21:36.330 --> 00:21:39.380
We are geniuses, after all...

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:47.920
Yeah, that's right.

00:22:09.710 --> 00:22:10.830
We are geniuses!

00:22:10.830 --> 00:22:11.960
The two of us are geniuses!

00:22:11.960 --> 00:22:13.080
Geniuses!

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:14.210
We're geniuses!

00:22:14.210 --> 00:22:15.710
Geniuses!

00:22:15.710 --> 00:22:17.920
What is with those two?

00:22:17.920 --> 00:22:18.420
Geniuses!

00:22:18.420 --> 00:22:19.880
Geniuses, eh?!

00:22:21.630 --> 00:22:23.960
We are geniuses!

00:22:28.750 --> 00:22:31.210
The trouble that led to that major incident...

00:22:31.960 --> 00:22:35.630
wasn't really taken up by anyone as a big problem.

00:22:36.880 --> 00:22:40.290
In terms of who saw Six act to prevent
the accident before it happened,

00:22:40.710 --> 00:22:44.330
it was just myself and a few others.

00:22:56.750 --> 00:22:58.000
Good night.

00:24:31.500 --> 00:24:37.290
Bewusstsein: an AI that has a sense of self,
which makes Six a robot who has a heart!

00:24:37.460 --> 00:24:40.000
With that in mind, I hope the
regular briefing session goes well...

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.500
The A106 model is the strongest robot around!

00:24:42.500 --> 00:24:46.750
He can output a whole 1,000 horsepower,
and he's got a killer high-speed Beat Punch!

00:24:46.750 --> 00:24:48.630
You think that appeal of yours
is going to land us research funding?

00:24:48.630 --> 00:24:51.000
It'll be alright. We're geniuses, after all.

00:24:51.000 --> 00:24:52.500
Next time on ATOM THE BEGINNING:

00:24:52.500 --> 00:24:53.210
"Bewusstsein"

00:24:53.210 --> 00:24:55.830
A106, boot up!
